blip: third-party licenses
==========================

blip is licensed under the MIT license. It includes the following third-party software.

This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Gaia DR3 (embedded star catalog)

This work has made use of data from the European Space Agency (ESA) mission Gaia
(https://www.cosmos.esa.int/gaia), processed by the Gaia Data Processing and Analysis
Consortium (DPAC, https://www.cosmos.esa.int/web/gaia/dpac/consortium). Funding for the
DPAC has been provided by national institutions, in particular the institutions
participating in the Gaia Multilateral Agreement.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OpenNGC (embedded deep-sky object list)

Deep-sky object data from OpenNGC (https://github.com/mattiaverga/OpenNGC) by
Mattia Verga, licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
International license (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).
The data was modified: reduced to a subset of columns, stars, duplicates and
nonexistent objects as well as faint galaxies without a common name were left
out, and it was converted to a tab-separated format. The modified data is
distributed under the same license.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Linked web services

blip can open AstroBin, Aladin Lite and SIMBAD in the web browser. It contains
no data from these services. AstroBin is a trademark of its owner; Aladin Lite
and SIMBAD are operated by CDS, Strasbourg Astronomical Observatory, France.
blip is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by any of them; their
names are used only to refer to their services.

